<title>USA: Encryption export bill backed in U.S. Senate.</title>
<headline>Encryption export bill backed in U.S. Senate.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bipartisan group of U.S. Senators on Tuesday endorsed a bill to promote U.S. exports of encryption technology by removing government barriers on foreign sales.</p>
<p>&quot;Foreign companies are fully utilizing this technology, while Americans companies have their hands tied with draconian U.S. laws on encryption,&quot; Sen. John Ashcroft, R-Missouri, said.</p>
<p>He joined Sens Conrad Burns, R-Montana and Patrick Leahy, D-Vermont in endorsing the Promotion of Commerce Online in the Digital Era (PRO-CODE) bill.</p>
</text>
